  "title": "Polyarrythmia — Highlight Reel",
  "summary": "This exhibition by electronic musician Jan St. Werner places audio on par with visual art. Nine compositions, released as NFTs via Feral File, form *Polyarrythmia*. St. Werner describes it as \"a narrative in sound\" without a strict metronome, featuring interlocking peaks, micro-moments, and larger arcs. Mastered for intensity and maximum resolution, the pieces were constructed in relation to each other.\n\nSt. Werner envisions *Polyarrythmia* with \"cabaret connotations\" and as a \"symphony of unknown instruments,\" encouraging a reconsideration of sound and perception. He views digital art as a manifestation of thoughts, with the output—whether visual or sonic—expressing an artist's response to the world.\n\nFor St. Werner, digital art offers an intuitive way to interface with the world. NFTs present new possibilities for intense, sensual, and direct communication. He sees the digital realm as a space for poetic, experimental, or critical expression, and a territory requiring the formulation of alternatives and openings against surveillance and manipulation.",
